Dear Emerus Patient Relations,

Attached is the email I received from INTEGRIS Health Patient Relations
referring this matter to Emerus Patient Relations and confirming that my
concerns have been forwarded to your office.

I am writing regarding my grandmother, Karen Sue Lafferty, who was treated
at the INTEGRIS Health Community Hospital operated by Emerus before being
transferred to Norman Regional HealthPlex.

*Patient Information:*

Karen Sue Lafferty
Date of Birth: March 16, 1948
Date of Death: April 22, 2026

I am requesting that a formal investigation be opened regarding my
grandmother's missing purse and personal belongings. Based on the
information currently available, her purse was present when she left one
facility but was missing after her transfer. Because there is concern that
property associated with her belongings may have been used without
authorization after her death, I respectfully request that this matter be
treated as time-sensitive.

Please provide the following:

   - A formal missing property investigation.
   - An incident or case number.
   - The name and contact information of the department or investigator
   assigned to this matter.
   - Copies of all documentation regarding my grandmother's personal
   belongings, including any property inventory, chain-of-custody records,
   transfer paperwork, and nursing notes referencing her belongings.
   - Documentation identifying what personal belongings accompanied her
   when she was transferred from your facility.
   - The name of the ambulance or medical transport company that
   transported her to Norman Regional HealthPlex, if available.
   - Preservation of any available surveillance video showing my
   grandmother's transfer, discharge, movement through the facility, ambulance
   loading area, and the handling of her personal belongings.
   - Preservation of any other relevant evidence, including photographs,
   electronic records, internal communications, reports, or logs related to
   her belongings or transfer.

I would also like instructions for obtaining all medical records related to
her visit and transfer from your facility. If documentation is required to
establish my authority to obtain records under applicable law, please let
me know exactly what is needed so I can provide it promptly.

Please confirm receipt of this email, advise when the investigation has
been opened, and provide the assigned case or incident number.

Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter. I look forward to your
response.

Sincerely,

Matthew Lafferty
Phone: (405) 802-0225
Email: blahtblclthpt99@gmail.com

